<speak>It sounds as though he is finding a thoughtful way to contribute, rather than merely taking tasks off your desk. A family business can benefit from that sort of conversation, provided everyone has space to explain what they are trying to achieve. We can apply the same patience to our administrative arrangements. If a particular contact method is not working for you, you can tell us what is inconvenient, and we can consider the practical options without treating it as a complaint. The relationship should not depend on you fitting all your personal administration around a hectic working day.</speak>